Add the two NXP TFA9874 speaker amplifier nodes to &i2c15, alongside the
FSA4480 that patch 0018 puts on that same bus.

Regenerated 2026-09-15 against the full series (through 0039), not reused
from the WSL prework tree: 0018 added fsa4480@42 inside this exact node, so
the original hunk no longer matched. Wiring is from the stock OxygenOS DTB
(MASTER 6.2): i2c15 0x34/0x35, reset tlmm 91/99 active-high, pm8150_s4 =
vreg_s4a_1p8, and no shutdown GPIOs exist on this board.

Carries both nxp,tfa-channel (read by the tfa2 driver, patch 0043) and
sound-channel (read by the tfa9872 driver, patch 0044), so either driver
binds to these nodes with no separate devicetree variant.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts
@@ -1576,6 +1576,44 @@
 			};
 		};
 	};
+
+	/*
+	 * NXP TFA9874 smart speaker amplifiers (TFA2 family), left and right.
+	 *
+	 * Verified against the stock OxygenOS DTB: this same i2c15 bus, 0x34 and
+	 * 0x35, reset on tlmm 91 / 99 active-high, both fed from pm8150_s4
+	 * (1.8 V, mainline vreg_s4a_1p8). The stock nodes carry reset-gpio only,
+	 * so there are no shutdown GPIOs to model on this board.
+	 *
+	 * Two channel properties are present deliberately: nxp,tfa-channel is
+	 * read by the tfa2 driver, sound-channel by the alternative tfa9872
+	 * driver, so either can bind to these nodes with no separate DT variant.
+	 */
+	tfa9874_left: speaker-amp@34 {
+		compatible = "nxp,tfa9874";
+		reg = <0x34>;
+
+		vddd-supply = <&vreg_s4a_1p8>;
+		reset-gpios = <&tlmm 91 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+
+		nxp,tfa-channel = <0>;
+		sound-channel = <0>;
+
+		#sound-dai-cells = <0>;
+	};
+
+	tfa9874_right: speaker-amp@35 {
+		compatible = "nxp,tfa9874";
+		reg = <0x35>;
+
+		vddd-supply = <&vreg_s4a_1p8>;
+		reset-gpios = <&tlmm 99 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+
+		nxp,tfa-channel = <1>;
+		sound-channel = <1>;
+
+		#sound-dai-cells = <0>;
+	};
 };
 
